INT. CONVERTED LIGHTHOUSE - COWORKING SPACE - DAY

A spiral staircase of standing desks. Fresnel lens turned into a conference light. Everyone wears matching grey fleece.

BARNABY STOKES (40s, community manager, smiling too hard) claps once at the top of the stairs. ORLA FITZGIBBON (30s, product lead, cold brew) leans on the rail. JUNG-HO PARK (20s, engineer, noise-cancelling headphones) types. ADAEZE NWOSU (30s, designer, sketchbook) draws the lens. CEDRIC LAMONT (50s, investor, borrowed lanyard) examines the view like a purchase.

BARNABY
(to everyone)
Hi, team! Quick announcement: we are pivoting.

Nobody moves. Jung-Ho slides one headphone off an ear.

JUNG-HO
To what?

BARNABY
To the next thing.

ORLA
We pivoted Tuesday.

ADAEZE
(muttering)
We pivoted into a wall.

CEDRIC
(to Barnaby)
Walk me through the vision.

BARNABY
It's a platform for platforms.

Orla and Jung-Ho speak at the same moment.

ORLA
That's not a product.

JUNG-HO
That's a typo.

BARNABY
(to Orla)
I need you aligned.

ORLA
I'm aligned. I'm so aligned I'm sideways.

Cedric descends two steps and peers at Adaeze's sketchbook.

CEDRIC
Is that the logo?

ADAEZE
It's a lighthouse.

CEDRIC
We should keep that.

She closes the book very slowly.

ADAEZE
(to herself)
It was always the lighthouse.

BARNABY
(to everyone)
So! Who's excited?

A long pause. The lens rotates. A single pigeon lands on the rail. Jung-Ho raises one hand.

JUNG-HO
Can I be excused?

BARNABY
It's a flat org.

JUNG-HO
Then I flatly would like to leave.
